      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142449",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/0b/0b5037831d90f93fb6b8b0603655162e4f362a638b35c569f7c5e07007974b3d.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 16$ from a normal population. Given that the sample mean is $50$, and the sample standard deviation is $8$, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\u03bc$ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 1.753) = 0.05$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $15$ degrees of freedom, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
